# Test conventions

Tests live in `src/tests/<domain>.test.ts` or alongside source as `<file>.test.ts`.

## Infrastructure

- `src/tests/setup.ts` is loaded by Jest automatically (`setupFilesAfterFramework` in `jest.config.js`)
- It starts an in-memory MongoDB via `mongodb-memory-server`, connects Mongoose, and clears all collections `afterEach`
- **Do NOT add `beforeAll`/`afterAll` for MongoDB** in test files — `setup.ts` handles it

## App import

```typescript
import app from '../app';     // default export = createApp() result — do NOT call createApp() yourself
import request from 'supertest';
```

## HTTP assertions

```typescript
const res = await request(app)
  .post('/api/events')
  .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`)
  .send({ title: 'Test Race', date: '2025-09-01', capacity: 50 })
  .expect(201);

expect(res.body).toMatchObject({ success: true, data: { title: 'Test Race' } });
```

## Data seeding

Seed via Mongoose models directly — never via API:
```typescript
import { Event } from '../models/Event';
await Event.create({ title: 'Seeded Race', date: new Date('2025-09-01'), capacity: 100 });
```

## Auth tokens

```typescript
import jwt from 'jsonwebtoken';
import { jwtConfig } from '../config/env';

const token = jwt.sign({ userId: 'someId', isAdmin: false }, jwtConfig.accessSecret, { expiresIn: '1h' });
```

## Jest facts

- Timeout: 10 000 ms
- `forceExit: true` — no hanging processes
- `clearMocks`, `resetMocks`, `restoreMocks` all `true` — mocks reset between tests

## Do not

- Seed data via API calls (POST /api/...) — seed via Mongoose models
- Import and call `createApp()` — use the default `app` import
- Leave `console.log` in committed tests
- Write tests that depend on document insertion order without explicit `.sort()`
